{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR-1, the room deployment files matched to the reviewed Worker policies, at exact head 8da61f7d231600e11116b51daae1c34c1d10c819, tree 590a7eee64b584a3cfab802758c05618fb45add8, on builder/br1-deploy-policy-20261025 (review request c567d710, my promise ae954bb6). This review binds request 3e836613 (builder promise 06d1084c; tech-debt review 72a6df7d findings TD-01, TD-02, TD-03 and TD-12; planner decision PD-8) to this one candidate. The head may land on Main d5e55530: it sits directly on Main (three commits, fast-forward, git merge-tree returns the head's own tree), and gate 75445 at e8ec5a8b stands under the documents-only rule because the head differs from the gated commit only in the implementation note (+12/-2, one path).\n\nRead order: the primary note first and in full, then the review request, the BR-1 request and the four findings it cites with PD-8, then the nine supporting artifacts as the full diff against Main (three room files, the CLI config test, the Scope test compiler config, the entry-point check, the entry-point inventory, docs/deploy.md and the Grow runbook), then the creation-pin parser the files feed, then the bound evidence index and the gate, affected and control records it names.\n\nHead checks: the worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-br1-deploy-policy-20261025 is clean at the head on its branch; 10 files, +160/-12; git diff --check is clean; check-commit-messages reports 3 checked, 0 flagged; the 10 artifact acts at this head name exactly the 10 changed paths. The nine implementation paths are byte-identical at 4f26e1d9 (the affected checkpoint), e8ec5a8b (the gated checkpoint) and this head.\n\nAcceptance, checked against the request:\n- Index mode. wrangler.grow.jsonc and wrangler.lending.jsonc now set SCOPE_INDEX_MODE to enforce, the mode both Workers have run in since 23 October by the sprint reports and the planner's deploy records (TD-01); wrangler.demo.jsonc already had it. A literal deploy from the file can no longer reopen register mode. The generic artroom-scope file keeps register mode and no allowance, as TD-13 decided, and the config test pins that too.\n- Allowances. Each of the three files carries PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS with the exact six-pin family PD-8 assigned: register 17, directory 16, membership 8, rules 10, destination 12 and inbox 1 for dap-demo and dap-grow; register 5, directory 5, membership 4, rules 3, destination 2 and inbox 1 for dap-lending. I read the parser at the head (creation-versions.ts): it refuses non-string, oversize, non-array, over-128, duplicate-within-list and unknown pins, and unions the accepted list with the newest cohort through a Set, so pins shared with the newest cohort (membership 8, rules 10, inbox 1) are accepted and deduplicated rather than refused. My own probe through that parser at the head, run as a temporary Vitest file in the cli project and removed afterwards (1.04 s wall): all three strings parse to a policy; the effective sets are 9 pins for dap-demo and dap-grow and 11 for dap-lending; every listed pin and the newest register 18 are permitted, an unlisted historical family (register 9) is not; the absent setting yields the newest six; a duplicated pin and an unknown pin are refused; artroom-scope has no allowance and register mode. The live dap-grow allowance was recorded by the planner as the register 17 allowance; its effective pin set equals this file's whether the live string lists three pins or six, because the other three belong to the newest cohort. The index itself states the provenance honestly: PD-8 and local file comparison, no fresh hosted probe.\n- --keep-vars. At the head, git grep for deploy commands outside notes/ finds eight room or Grow commands, and every one carries --keep-vars (both room file headers, docs/deploy.md for Grow and the new dap-demo section, the runbook at lines 25, 272 and 359, and the deploy:scope script). The only deploy command without it is deploy:home for the homepage Worker, which is not a room deployment. docs/deploy.md keeps the correct statement that --keep-vars preserves only values the file omits and that explicit file values and --var still override.\n- worker.grow.ts type checked. packages/scope/tsconfig.test.json now includes ../../apps/room/worker.grow.ts; tsc -p on that config at the head exits 0 in my own run (0.64 s wall, TypeScript 7.0.2). The gate's typecheck stage ran 40 compiler contexts with no TypeScript error.\n- dap-demo in the entry-point check. scripts/security-entry-points.mjs adds the wrangler.demo.jsonc and worker.ts pair and the dap-demo heading; docs/security/entry-points.md gains the dap-demo table (34 route rows). node scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs passes 4 of 4 at the head in my own run (1.22 s wall), which is the bijection of the served inventory of seven Workers against the documented tables. The seal map is unchanged and the structural test's seal cases pass.\n- docs/deploy.md gains the dap-demo section with the exact planner command and states the three families, the additive parser semantics, the artroom-scope exception and that BR-1 neither replaces the fixed register 17 offer nor activates R7's register 19.\n\nQualified evidence, verified: the bound index (24,145 bytes, SHA256 e9cdd7bd…, as the artifact act states) names 35 files; the 26 absolute evidence files exist with the stated sizes and digests, and the nine repository paths carry the digests of the head's blobs. Gate 75445: the raw record has expectedHead e8ec5a8b, expectedTree a5d04fe8, exitCode 0, errors [], unreached []; the wrapper's log shows eight stages at exit 0, \"Tests 3585 passed | 3 skipped (3588)\" over 500 passed and 1 skipped files, Node 42 and Counting 55; the typecheck log holds 40 tsc invocations and no TypeScript error; the 17 stage copies are identical to their originals; before.json and after.json differ only in the Vitest results cache file and the Vite temp directory timestamps, not in any source. The independent audit (manifest 790 bytes, SHA256 17e9f7b2…) has three leaves and 63 input pins that all verify, its receipt (39,569 bytes, SHA256 aebc59ce…) records the same head and tree with the reconciliation passed. Affected run 65721 at 4f26e1d9: audit leaves and 45 pins verify; the phases are the cli and scope test compilers, the CLI config case 868011204_0 passed, seven Node whole files, 714 links with none broken, and the citation check. Control 59614: the mutant f0191770 removed only the 52-byte Demo servedInventory line; the first case failed on the Worker-tables assertion with the six-Worker served list against the seven-Worker documented list, two later cases failed consequentially and the fourth passed; the positive bytes were restored at 4f26e1d9 (24,712 bytes, SHA256 4b67b4be…, equal to the head's file); its audit's two leaves and 30 pins verify. I read these records and did not rerun them. Counting is Node coverage; no browser or hosted check is claimed and none ran.\n\nNonblocking notes: docs/security/entry-points.md now says the seven configurations are \"named by D1\", while D1 named six and dap-demo is the addition; \"the six named by D1 and dap-demo\" would be exact. The config test keeps its earlier explicit dap-demo name, main and mode assertion beside the new table that checks the same three values; one of the two could go. The runbook's simulator deploy (examples/grow/wrangler.jsonc) also gained --keep-vars; it is outside TD-01's four commands and harmless.\n\nArchitecture: the deployment policy lives in the three files that deployments read, with one config test as witness and the parser unchanged; the compiler root and the entry-point inventory each grow by one real entry. No new module, setting or code path.\n\nSecurity: a literal deploy of the Grow or Lending file now keeps enforce mode and preserves omitted settings, closing the TD-01 risk that a file-following deploy reopens register admission or drops MCP_ENABLED; the committed allowances admit exactly the historical families the registers already create, with the parser refusing unknown or duplicated pins; artroom-scope founds no new rooms and gets no allowance; dap-demo's routes are now under the gate-class bijection. No recorded bytes, scope pin, native declaration or seal change.\n\nSimplification: the duplicate dap-demo assertion in demo-config.test.ts; nothing else.\n\nFindings: none blocking. Landing is the builder's; redeploying the Workers from these files is the planner's, and the dap-demo root cutover stays R7's.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c8b80e03ff7e384e69fd9c1ce4690c595cd1d275","binding":"assigned","head":"8da61f7d231600e11116b51daae1c34c1d10c819","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ae954bb6ebae1fb3a423fbcdc131a6c3546e2230\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d1084c450cce3bf5b4dea35a6b54710bd4be2a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ede5f819a5ee58c82b4fe02ef9b4b70dadba846","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}